{
  "$schema": "https://vega.github.io/schema/vega-lite/v5.json",
  "description": "Scatter plot: household income vs household expenditure by state 2022",
  "width": "container",
  "height": 380,
  "data": {
    "url": "data/state_snapshot.csv"
  },
  "transform": [
    {
      "filter": "datum.state != 'W.P. Putrajaya'"
    }
  ],
  "layer": [
    {
      "mark": {
        "type": "point",
        "filled": true,
        "opacity": 0.85,
        "stroke": "var(--border)",
        "strokeWidth": 0.5
      },
      "encoding": {
        "x": {
          "field": "income_mean",
          "type": "quantitative",
          "title": "Mean Household Income (RM/month)",
          "scale": {
            "domain": [
              4000,
              14000
            ]
          },
          "axis": {
            "format": ","
          }
        },
        "y": {
          "field": "expenditure_mean",
          "type": "quantitative",
          "title": "Mean Household Expenditure (RM/month)",
          "scale": {
            "domain": [
              3000,
              9500
            ]
          },
          "axis": {
            "format": ","
          }
        },
        "size": {
          "field": "birth_rate",
          "type": "quantitative",
          "title": "Birth Rate (per 1,000)",
          "scale": {
            "range": [
              100,
              900
            ]
          },
          "legend": {
            "orient": "right",
            "titleFont": "JetBrains Mono",
            "titleFontSize": 10,
            "labelFont": "JetBrains Mono",
            "labelFontSize": 10
          }
        },
        "color": {
          "field": "income_group",
          "type": "nominal",
          "title": "Income Group",
          "scale": {
            "domain": [
              "Low (<5.5k)",
              "Middle (5.5–8k)",
              "High (>8k)"
            ],
            "range": [
              "var(--red)",
              "var(--accent)",
              "var(--blue)"
            ]
          },
          "legend": {
            "orient": "right",
            "titleFont": "JetBrains Mono",
            "titleFontSize": 10,
            "labelFont": "JetBrains Mono",
            "labelFontSize": 10
          }
        },
        "tooltip": [
          {
            "field": "state",
            "title": "State"
          },
          {
            "field": "income_mean",
            "title": "Mean Income (RM)",
            "format": ","
          },
          {
            "field": "expenditure_mean",
            "title": "Mean Expenditure (RM)",
            "format": ","
          },
          {
            "field": "birth_rate",
            "title": "Birth Rate",
            "format": ".1f"
          },
          {
            "field": "poverty",
            "title": "Poverty Rate (%)",
            "format": ".1f"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "values": [
          {"state": "Kelantan", "x": 4885, "y": 3505, "dx": 0, "dy": -18, "align": "center"},
          {"state": "Kedah", "x": 5550, "y": 3765, "dx": -14, "dy": 2, "align": "right"},
          {"state": "Perlis", "x": 5664, "y": 3834, "dx": 12, "dy": -10, "align": "left"},
          {"state": "Perak", "x": 5779, "y": 3903, "dx": -14, "dy": 12, "align": "right"},
          {"state": "Pahang", "x": 5777, "y": 4107, "dx": 0, "dy": -18, "align": "center"},
          {"state": "Sabah", "x": 6171, "y": 3342, "dx": 0, "dy": 22, "align": "center"},
          {"state": "Sarawak", "x": 6457, "y": 3915, "dx": 14, "dy": 6, "align": "left"},
          {"state": "Negeri Sembilan", "x": 6788, "y": 4678, "dx": -14, "dy": -8, "align": "right"},
          {"state": "Terengganu", "x": 7248, "y": 4796, "dx": 20, "dy": -10, "align": "left"},
          {"state": "Melaka", "x": 8057, "y": 5707, "dx": -14, "dy": 0, "align": "right"},
          {"state": "Pulau Pinang", "x": 8267, "y": 5322, "dx": -14, "dy": 10, "align": "right"},
          {"state": "W.P. Labuan", "x": 8250, "y": 4176, "dx": 0, "dy": -18, "align": "center"},
          {"state": "Johor", "x": 8517, "y": 5342, "dx": 14, "dy": 10, "align": "left"},
          {"state": "Selangor", "x": 12233, "y": 6770, "dx": -18, "dy": 0, "align": "right"},
          {"state": "W.P. Kuala Lumpur", "x": 13325, "y": 7823, "dx": 18, "dy": 0, "align": "left"}
        ]
      },
      "mark": {
        "type": "text",
        "fontSize": 9,
        "font": "JetBrains Mono",
        "color": "var(--muted)",
        "fontWeight": "bold"
      },
      "encoding": {
        "x": {
          "field": "x",
          "type": "quantitative"
        },
        "y": {
          "field": "y",
          "type": "quantitative"
        },
        "text": {
          "field": "state",
          "type": "nominal"
        },
        "dx": {
          "field": "dx",
          "type": "quantitative"
        },
        "dy": {
          "field": "dy",
          "type": "quantitative"
        },
        "align": {
          "field": "align",
          "type": "nominal"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "mark": {
        "type": "line",
        "color": "var(--border)",
        "strokeDash": [
          4,
          3
        ]
      },
      "transform": [
        {
          "regression": "expenditure_mean",
          "on": "income_mean"
        }
      ],
      "encoding": {
        "x": {
          "field": "income_mean",
          "type": "quantitative"
        },
        "y": {
          "field": "expenditure_mean",
          "type": "quantitative"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "values": [
          {
            "text": [
              "SOCIOECONOMIC INSIGHT: COST OF LIVING PRESSURE",
              "• Income vs. Spend: A near-linear correlation exists",
              "  between household income and expenditure across Malaysia.",
              "• The Childcare Trap: Developed states (KL, Selangor, Penang)",
              "  have high income, but high expenditure forces dual-income",
              "  households, leaving less time/resources for children.",
              "• Demographic Split: High-income states sit at the top-right",
              "  with smaller bubbles (low birth rates), while rural states",
              "  sit at the bottom-left with larger bubbles (high birth rates)."
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "mark": {
        "type": "text",
        "align": "left",
        "baseline": "top",
        "fontSize": 9,
        "font": "JetBrains Mono",
        "color": "var(--text)",
        "opacity": 0.85,
        "lineHeight": 14
      },
      "encoding": {
        "x": {
          "datum": 4200,
          "type": "quantitative"
        },
        "y": {
          "datum": 9300,
          "type": "quantitative"
        },
